{
  "id": "ss.relic.execute",
  "name": "Guillotine jaw",
  "description": "One mandible, hinged on a squared dark root at the top right and sickle-curved down to a point at the bottom left: dark amber chitin, a darker facet along its convex back, a bright line along the concave edge that does the cutting and two small inner teeth near the root, which are what make it a jaw and not a tusk. Under the point, a small pale stalk it has just gone through, in two square-ended pieces — the near half kicked away at an angle — because the relic is a finishing rule, not a bite, and the thing already severed is what says so. There is no second mandible and no head, so it does not read as a face or as the ss.relic.biggame trophy, which is a whole jaw at rest; this is a single blade in motion. The stalk is pale chitin rather than red so the icon stays a mechanism rather than a wound.",
